1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,060
Slide 9 analyzes "YESTERDAY: REACTIVE CHATBOTS."

2
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:23,390
On the left card, tagged "THE BOTTLENECK", we examine "Human as Middleware." For the last few years, whenever companies tried to implement AI, the human worker was forced to act as the physical bridge between ChatGPT, Google Docs, Slack, and email inboxes.

3
00:00:24,090 --> 00:00:41,920
Look at the right card tagged "THE COST": "High Latency & Fatigue." Because every single transaction required continuous human attention, professionals experienced massive cognitive fatigue, constant context switching, and high error rates from manual typing.

4
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:51,960
When you have to switch browser tabs 50 times an hour to copy-paste data, your brain cannot engage in deep creative problem solving or philosophical reflection.

5
00:00:52,660 --> 00:00:58,205
Chatbots gave us great text answers, but they left us chained to the keyboard.

6
00:00:58,205 --> 00:01:02,400
That is the mechanical bottleneck we are dismantling today.

